TinyML-Pareto patch for the Arduino library Chirale_TensorFLowLite 2.0.0 (the board's TFLM runtime, firmware/VERSIONS.md).
It makes the board's int8 arithmetic match TensorFlow 2.18 (the converter and host reference) bit for bit.

1. FULLY_CONNECTED, int8 with per-channel weights (micro/kernels/cmsis_nn/fully_connected.cpp).
   TF >= 2.16 quantizes dense weights with one scale per output neuron. Chirale 2.0.0 requantized every neuron with
   the first neuron's scale. Now the per-neuron multipliers and shifts are computed in Prepare
   (PopulateConvolutionQuantizationParams, as for CONV_2D) and the layer runs through VecMatMultPerChannelS8, a copy
   of CMSIS-NN 4.0.2's arm_nn_vec_mat_mult_t_s8 (the kernel behind arm_fully_connected_s8, SMLAD on Cortex-M4) that
   requantizes each output row with its own multiplier and shift. Per-tensor weights (one scale) keep the original
   arm_fully_connected_s8 path.
   (Version int8v2. Version int8 ran per-channel layers through the 1x1-convolution path, arm_convolve_1x1_s8_fast;
   the outputs are identical, but that path is 1.4-2.5x slower for a single input vector.)
2. MEAN, int8/int16 (micro/kernels/reduce_common.cpp).
   Chirale 2.0.0 rounds a float mean, or truncates an integer mean when input and output quantization are equal.
   TFLite 2.18 uses one integer path (reference_ops::QuantizedMeanOrSum, 1/n folded into the fixed-point
   multiplier); it is ported here. floor(log2 n) is computed directly because Chirale's CountLeadingZeros is
   32-bit only.

Float models are not affected (their code paths are unchanged).
Apply / check / revert: python tools/chirale_lib.py apply | status | revert   (tools/build_flash.py refuses to build
a TFLM bundle unless the installed library matches the patched tree hash in firmware/patches/chirale.json).

